WEBVTT

00:02.940 --> 00:04.360
<i>Cenancle Island.</i>

00:05.190 --> 00:07.360
<i>Population, approximately 42,000.</i>

00:07.360 --> 00:11.620
<i>The surface and underside of a high-tech island that's forever changing, day and night.</i>

00:11.620 --> 00:14.240
<i>The twisted crimes that take place within its folds.</i>

00:14.660 --> 00:17.210
<i>And the one and only young star who stands up to them.</i>

00:21.750 --> 00:22.880
Hello.

00:23.290 --> 00:25.710
This is Titan TV's production department.

00:25.710 --> 00:30.720
I'm calling in regards to our offer the other day to make you a regular on <i>Hyperion News</i>.

00:31.430 --> 00:32.680
<i>Success!</i>

00:33.100 --> 00:37.020
An idol that isn't popular is as no better than a pig, you know.

00:37.020 --> 00:40.520
And daily coverage costs are no joke.

00:41.190 --> 00:42.440
Hah, in your face!

00:42.770 --> 00:44.270
I accept!

00:44.270 --> 00:46.280
Relay the details to my agent.

00:46.280 --> 00:48.190
Thank you very much!

00:48.190 --> 00:51.200
You were our first choice after all, Ms. Sandra Jarny.

00:51.200 --> 00:52.160
That's not me!

00:52.160 --> 00:54.660
Of all people, <i>she</i> works for a rival company!

00:54.660 --> 00:56.700
Listen! My name is Vli—

00:55.790 --> 00:56.700
My apologies!

02:31.010 --> 02:33.090
Sheesh...

02:33.090 --> 02:37.510
She just underwent full maintenance the other day and now she's damaged herself again.

02:38.260 --> 02:43.100
How many times do you have to get hurt on the island before you're satisfied, Nene?

02:43.100 --> 02:45.020
And it's all because she keeps helping people.

02:46.150 --> 02:48.900
She falls out of trees fetching balloons for kids.

02:49.940 --> 02:52.440
She helps carry things, only to end up <i>beneath</i> them.

02:53.740 --> 02:56.360
She sewer dives to rescue a cat.

02:57.990 --> 03:03.790
Uzal apparently reinforced the bio-safety parts of her frame, so she hasn't been seriously hurt yet, but...

03:04.080 --> 03:05.790
But it ticks me off!

03:06.330 --> 03:08.290
And then there's this module she added!

03:08.290 --> 03:11.710
Pains me to admit it, but I've got no clue what the heck it is!

03:13.880 --> 03:19.050
Knowing that idiot, it's nothing that'll harm Nene, but it still triggers me!

03:19.050 --> 03:20.930
Today's the day...

03:21.260 --> 03:23.930
I put this mystery to bed!

03:29.270 --> 03:31.070
What's up, Clarin?

03:32.480 --> 03:34.820
Oh, you've got bed head.

03:34.820 --> 03:35.820
Leave it to me!

03:36.450 --> 03:38.570
Silky, smooth, and straight.

03:40.580 --> 03:43.330
<i>They won't detect me with today's Gertsecomma.</i>

03:43.330 --> 03:45.830
<i>It's got a direct cable connection!</i>

03:46.120 --> 03:48.880
Hey Clarin, thanks for everything.

03:48.880 --> 03:52.340
When I'm with you, I feel like I can do <i>anything</i>.

03:52.920 --> 03:54.760
Sorry I get so reckless.

03:54.760 --> 03:56.010
No problem.

03:56.010 --> 03:58.840
Clarion helps Nene do what she wants to do.

03:58.840 --> 04:00.760
Yeah! Thanks!

04:00.760 --> 04:03.720
Also, about when I transform...

04:04.060 --> 04:05.350
Transform!?

04:06.850 --> 04:09.100
What does <i>that</i> mean?

04:09.400 --> 04:10.690
Transform?

04:10.690 --> 04:15.860
Uh, you know, when you let me use your power and then everything gets all weightless.

04:16.570 --> 04:18.610
That's not a transformation.

04:18.610 --> 04:22.370
It's a response Uzal programmed to activate when we connect.

04:22.370 --> 04:24.740
She said it's a matter of taste.

04:24.740 --> 04:25.870
Taste?

04:27.870 --> 04:30.580
And after that, there's that flash of light.

04:31.420 --> 04:34.710
I believe I now understand what you mean by "transform."

04:34.710 --> 04:37.880
That's something that's set to occur when the optical camouflage activates.

04:38.170 --> 04:39.800
Optical camouflage!?

04:39.800 --> 04:41.640
On Nene's body!?

04:41.930 --> 04:44.140
Optical... camouflage?

04:44.600 --> 04:48.060
When it shines, it's examining your current appearance.

04:48.060 --> 04:49.690
What about when my clothes disappear?

04:49.690 --> 04:52.150
It's making your base clothing invisible.

04:52.690 --> 04:57.150
Optical camouflage is essentially a way to render something unseeable.

04:57.150 --> 04:58.280
I see.

04:58.280 --> 05:00.860
You can't change clothes
without undressing, after all.

05:00.860 --> 05:03.990
For some reason these occurrences don't happen all at once.

05:04.660 --> 05:06.740
For reasons unknown.

05:06.740 --> 05:09.410
Then the lights go all crazy again...

05:13.460 --> 05:15.500
and I'm done changing clothes!

05:15.500 --> 05:17.550
It just appears that way on the outside.

05:17.960 --> 05:20.720
Can I use it to choose clothes I like even better?

05:20.720 --> 05:21.720
Uncertain.

05:21.720 --> 05:24.430
I hope I can get to choose a signature pose too!

05:24.430 --> 05:25.300
Uncertain.

05:25.300 --> 05:27.770
<i>A disguise via optical camouflage?</i>

05:27.770 --> 05:31.940
<i>Come to think of it, Nene </i>has<i> looked different a few times.</i>

05:31.940 --> 05:35.060
I have a message in regards to this question.

05:35.520 --> 05:37.110
Yoo-hoo, Nene!

05:37.110 --> 05:38.440
Oh, Uzal!

05:38.440 --> 05:41.700
Transformations and signature poses are the marks of justice!

05:41.700 --> 05:43.700
They rock!

05:43.700 --> 05:49.330
Also, I swiped that 2001 prototype optical camouflage from Korobase and modded it.

05:49.330 --> 05:50.910
Don't let 'er know!

05:50.910 --> 05:55.460
Don't steal somebody's top-secret tech and then ruin it with your stupid tastes!

05:55.460 --> 05:58.050
She's always so selfish!

05:58.050 --> 05:59.960
Stare...

06:05.140 --> 06:06.600
At the end of the last century,

06:06.600 --> 06:12.730
the impact of a giant meteorite caused a spread of misinformation and the subsequent Asian Conflict.

06:14.060 --> 06:18.730
The former Japanese capital of Tokyo was devastated, and even now...

06:22.990 --> 06:24.910
Thanks for waiting, Clarin.

06:26.700 --> 06:27.620
Let's go.

06:31.370 --> 06:35.170
It's like, there's still so much I don't know.

06:35.170 --> 06:37.250
You wanna take online classes too, Clarin?

06:37.250 --> 06:38.250
Pass.

06:38.250 --> 06:39.380
What about you, BUER?

06:39.380 --> 06:43.510
<i>Mine</i> inquiring mind wisheth to learn about a maiden's secret pla—

06:45.180 --> 06:46.140
"Pass."

06:51.560 --> 06:52.640
Lookie there!

06:53.390 --> 06:56.350
It's still being built, but wouldn't you call it first-class?

06:56.350 --> 06:57.400
Yup!

06:57.400 --> 07:00.650
Now we can say goodbye to living in that puny tent!

07:01.150 --> 07:04.530
I'll make a house for you too, tiny thingy!

07:05.910 --> 07:10.200
None may confine me to a dark place!

07:18.080 --> 07:20.250
Oh! Robert!

07:20.540 --> 07:22.170
Yo, Nene.

07:22.170 --> 07:23.010
Clarin.

07:23.010 --> 07:24.590
Clarion.

07:24.590 --> 07:26.380
Do you live here too?

07:26.380 --> 07:28.890
Nah, I just stopped by to help out.

07:28.890 --> 07:30.430
Oh, I see.

07:32.220 --> 07:34.140
Well, it's in my nature.

07:40.650 --> 07:42.190
Hello, Captain!

07:42.190 --> 07:43.900
Good work, men.

07:45.360 --> 07:48.950
The forced relocation has the citizens worried,

07:48.950 --> 07:53.580
and we've got mysterious network outages and android thefts to deal with as well.

07:54.290 --> 07:56.290
Stay focused and alert.

07:56.290 --> 07:57.120
Yes, sir!

08:20.900 --> 08:24.820
Two high-grade androids spotted right on time with the intel.

08:24.820 --> 08:27.110
They're unaccompanied by their owner.

08:27.400 --> 08:30.530
This is why you stake out the rich part of the city.

08:30.530 --> 08:34.080
Find shit on the sidewalks around here worth more than luxury cars!

08:34.080 --> 08:36.120
Aww, they're holding hands!

08:36.120 --> 08:37.620
And two of 'em! Awesome!

08:37.620 --> 08:39.870
As long as they're worth good grub.

08:40.880 --> 08:41.500
Oh!

08:42.880 --> 08:44.840
Welcome back, CoCCo!

08:44.840 --> 08:46.510
Good job out there!

08:46.880 --> 08:48.550
Ready, boys!?

08:48.550 --> 08:51.760
Intel says were 'bout to have an outage!

08:52.300 --> 08:55.770
I doubt the CDF cares about a couple 'a petty thieves,

08:55.770 --> 08:58.270
but don't get sloppy and leave evidence out there!

08:58.270 --> 09:00.020
Let's do this, boys!

09:12.240 --> 09:13.490
It blocked them!?

09:13.490 --> 09:15.700
The one with the ears must be a guard!

09:15.700 --> 09:17.120
Be careful!

09:17.120 --> 09:18.620
What? What!?

09:18.620 --> 09:20.080
Robbers!

09:20.080 --> 09:22.170
Return, fiends!

09:22.170 --> 09:25.170
Unable to report.

09:29.800 --> 09:32.380
Damn it, shit's not hitting!

09:32.380 --> 09:34.680
That one's the guard, all right.

09:34.680 --> 09:36.060
Mr. Fried!

09:37.930 --> 09:39.520
Search for refuge.

09:39.520 --> 09:40.270
Clarin!

09:40.270 --> 09:41.480
Me too!

09:50.570 --> 09:52.780
What's takin' you boys so long?

09:52.780 --> 09:54.910
Let's wrap this up already!

09:54.910 --> 09:56.280
Mr. Chicken!

10:10.670 --> 10:13.050
Don't scratch it, Lil' Bro!

10:13.970 --> 10:14.890
Mhm.

10:20.810 --> 10:22.180
Good! It's airborne!

10:23.640 --> 10:25.560
Capture nets, aim!

10:25.560 --> 10:26.900
Fire!

10:33.780 --> 10:35.450
This one's heavy.

10:35.780 --> 10:37.280
We caught it, huh?

10:37.280 --> 10:38.950
Whoa!

10:38.950 --> 10:40.580
It's armed?

10:40.580 --> 10:42.330
Maybe it's more than we can handle.

10:42.330 --> 10:44.000
Mr. Chicken!

10:44.000 --> 10:46.000
The outage is almost up!

10:46.000 --> 10:47.330
We'll get reported!

10:48.380 --> 10:50.210
It sucks, but oh well.

10:50.210 --> 10:53.220
Hurry and shield that one I dropped.

10:53.220 --> 10:54.470
We just need the humanoid one.

10:54.760 --> 10:56.470
Okay.

10:56.840 --> 10:58.550
Hurry, hurry!

11:08.520 --> 11:10.270
Ye lot are lucky!

11:10.270 --> 11:12.230
I shall let thee go, for today!

11:23.500 --> 11:27.500
I thought the connection died all of the sudden, but it was actually a network outage!

11:27.500 --> 11:30.290
And, to make matters worse, Nene disappeared!

11:30.290 --> 11:32.250
Why can't I find her signal!?

11:34.380 --> 11:35.470
Hey, wait!

11:35.470 --> 11:37.510
What's the matter, puppet!?

11:37.890 --> 11:39.640
Show me your logs.

11:41.720 --> 11:43.770
Nene was abducted!?

11:44.100 --> 11:48.100
These guys think they can make a fool of me!?

11:50.310 --> 11:53.780
They must be shielding Nene's signal.

11:53.780 --> 11:57.070
But if they're using a vehicle...

11:57.070 --> 11:59.530
Searching island traffic database.

11:59.910 --> 12:01.950
Analyzing surveillance camera footage.

12:01.950 --> 12:03.370
Narrowing down matches.

12:06.750 --> 12:08.170
I found it!

12:09.540 --> 12:13.250
They're AI thieves who have been working the island lately!

12:13.250 --> 12:18.180
It's no surprise they'd zero in on Nene and the puppet.

12:18.180 --> 12:20.640
I hid those two flawlessly,

12:20.640 --> 12:24.810
but it was careless of me not to consider petty thieves!

12:25.270 --> 12:30.440
If <i>she</i> ever finds out Nene was put in danger over something so dumb...

12:30.440 --> 12:32.230
You moron!

12:37.150 --> 12:40.530
I'll take them down before it's reported to the CDF!

12:40.530 --> 12:41.780
All Gertsecommas!

12:42.370 --> 12:45.080
Deploy with extermination-type equipment!

12:45.080 --> 12:46.120
Hey, puppet!

12:46.120 --> 12:49.830
Stand down and rendezvous with my forces!

12:51.210 --> 12:52.840
Hey!

12:54.840 --> 12:56.090
Get on.

12:57.460 --> 12:59.760
Fly like the wind, puppet!

13:00.930 --> 13:02.140
How cute!

13:02.140 --> 13:03.100
You're heavy.

13:03.100 --> 13:04.470
What's that?

13:04.470 --> 13:05.720
Cool!

13:06.060 --> 13:07.180
Huh?

13:07.180 --> 13:08.350
Clarin?

13:28.410 --> 13:30.500
This must be the place.

13:31.040 --> 13:33.750
We'll do recon until my reinforcements arrive.

13:35.420 --> 13:37.920
We'll figure out where Nene is first.

13:37.920 --> 13:39.920
Then our plan will depend on what we—

13:41.630 --> 13:43.010
I got cut off again!?

13:44.680 --> 13:48.020
I never thought you'd actually follow us.

13:48.020 --> 13:49.850
We welcome ya.

13:50.680 --> 13:52.900
Good job, CoCCo.

13:52.900 --> 13:55.940
Now... let the games begin.

13:58.780 --> 14:01.900
We'll settle this before the CDF gets here.

14:03.910 --> 14:05.780
Feast upon mine goat hooves.

14:10.040 --> 14:10.790
What's up?

14:11.370 --> 14:13.210
Trespasser, apparently.

14:13.210 --> 14:14.920
Just leave that one over there.

14:23.680 --> 14:24.550
Huh?

14:28.180 --> 14:30.430
It's cramped in here!

14:32.560 --> 14:34.310
I'm out!

14:34.310 --> 14:36.860
What happened to me, anyway?

14:38.570 --> 14:39.780
Where am I?

14:41.820 --> 14:44.110
H-Hello...

14:49.870 --> 14:50.950
Oh, right!

14:50.950 --> 14:52.370
Where's Clarin?

15:00.170 --> 15:03.340
If we've been traced, we'll have to move to a new hideout.

15:05.090 --> 15:07.800
Well, it was about time we did anyway.

15:07.800 --> 15:08.720
Fine by me.

15:09.220 --> 15:12.310
Worth this quality catch.

15:13.640 --> 15:15.850
Hurry up and nab it, Fried!

15:15.850 --> 15:17.480
Don't goin bustin' it up!

15:21.440 --> 15:22.320
Bro...

15:22.320 --> 15:24.280
This one's quick!

15:25.280 --> 15:28.820
Man, you're always rushin' straight in.

15:28.820 --> 15:34.750
An android without its owner's just
a mindless puppet that protects itself!

15:52.310 --> 15:53.810
Good job!

15:53.810 --> 15:55.730
Now take down its system!

15:57.640 --> 16:00.860
It's just some rich person's toy, in the end.

16:05.360 --> 16:07.110
Don't struggle.

16:24.090 --> 16:25.510
Mr. Fried!

16:25.510 --> 16:30.430
Th-This fuckin' android attacked
a human without being ordered to!

16:31.010 --> 16:32.550
It's g-got an illegal AI!

16:33.890 --> 16:36.560
You mechanical bitch!

16:36.560 --> 16:38.940
You wrecked my brother's arm!

16:38.940 --> 16:40.020
Break it!

16:40.310 --> 16:42.230
Destroy it!

16:42.230 --> 16:43.520
Go get the guns!

16:47.400 --> 16:48.700
Clarin!

16:52.950 --> 16:54.280
Hey!

16:54.280 --> 16:56.160
Clarin!

16:58.160 --> 17:00.040
Hey, hold it!

17:00.040 --> 17:01.710
It's a-a-awake!?

17:01.710 --> 17:04.290
Why'd you go and start it up on your own, stupid!?

17:04.290 --> 17:05.500
I didn't!

17:05.500 --> 17:07.550
What's goin' on?

17:08.130 --> 17:09.470
Clarin!

17:09.470 --> 17:11.550
You came to get me!

17:11.550 --> 17:12.760
Thanks.

17:12.760 --> 17:14.300
This place is dangerous.

17:14.300 --> 17:15.970
Evacuation recommended.

17:15.970 --> 17:17.810
Yeah! Let's go home!

17:17.810 --> 17:20.940
Oh... but hang on, Clarin.

17:25.070 --> 17:28.740
There are a bunch of people I want to take with us.

17:28.740 --> 17:31.660
But they can't move because they're empty.

17:31.660 --> 17:33.120
Empty?

17:33.120 --> 17:34.200
Yeah...

17:34.200 --> 17:37.660
But they're all saying they want to go home.

17:39.080 --> 17:40.410
They want to go home?

17:41.000 --> 17:42.540
So, please.

17:42.540 --> 17:46.170
Clarin, help me just a little.

17:50.590 --> 17:51.720
Understood.

17:57.760 --> 18:01.480
Pandora Device, open!

18:07.020 --> 18:08.980
Set up in front of the door!

18:08.980 --> 18:10.740
It's the only way in or out!

18:10.740 --> 18:12.490
Trapped like a rat!

18:13.030 --> 18:15.240
Do your thing, CoCCo!

18:17.240 --> 18:22.710
I guess it's quite a catch if it's got a dangerous illegal AI like that guardin' it, huh?

18:24.040 --> 18:25.960
Don't feel bad, Fried.

18:25.960 --> 18:29.300
We'll sell it off, and get you some high-grade arms.

18:29.300 --> 18:30.760
Bro...

18:31.170 --> 18:34.760
We'll move in once CoCCo takes out its sensors.

18:35.050 --> 18:37.350
Don't damage the loot.

18:37.350 --> 18:39.140
Destroy the one with the ears!

18:49.650 --> 18:51.780
What's the matter, CoCCo?

18:59.120 --> 19:00.330
Why!?

19:00.330 --> 19:01.910
CoCCo!

19:01.910 --> 19:03.960
C-Can't see!

19:03.960 --> 19:06.040
Who's there!? Let me go!

19:06.040 --> 19:06.880
Damn it!

19:06.880 --> 19:08.170
What's with these guys!?

19:08.540 --> 19:10.500
What's wrong with you guys!?

19:10.500 --> 19:12.170
The hell's happening!?

19:13.840 --> 19:15.090
Keep away!

19:16.050 --> 19:17.680
S-Stop it!

19:17.680 --> 19:20.430
Quit... crushin' me!

19:20.430 --> 19:22.270
Let me go! Shit!

19:22.270 --> 19:24.180
I can't move!

19:24.180 --> 19:26.980
Wh-Why did these things start up!?

19:26.980 --> 19:28.610
Let me go!

19:30.570 --> 19:33.280
We reformatted them,
so why are they moving around!?

19:33.280 --> 19:35.030
Goddammit!

19:35.780 --> 19:36.950
Clarin...

19:37.280 --> 19:39.950
Clarin... Clarin...

19:41.660 --> 19:44.450
Clarin... Clarin... Clarin...

19:41.910 --> 19:44.450
Wh-What the hell?

19:45.620 --> 19:46.870
We're surrounded!

19:46.870 --> 19:48.080
Put me down!

19:48.080 --> 19:49.460
What're they doing!?

19:50.290 --> 19:53.880
Decode skill, Elpis Series!

19:55.050 --> 19:56.260
Please don't...

19:56.260 --> 19:58.300
...be mean to Clarin.

19:59.720 --> 20:00.850
Puppeteer!

20:10.270 --> 20:11.570
What's goin' on here!?

20:11.570 --> 20:12.730
Let us go!

20:12.730 --> 20:14.110
Damn it!

20:14.110 --> 20:15.490
Just don't...

20:15.490 --> 20:18.780
Just don't hurt my brother!

20:20.620 --> 20:22.160
CoCCo!

20:28.250 --> 20:30.040
Mhm. Mhm.

20:30.580 --> 20:32.590
Sorry I made you do that.

20:32.590 --> 20:33.960
You want to go home, right?

20:42.850 --> 20:43.760
CoCCo?

20:44.260 --> 20:46.850
I'm returning your chicken.

20:46.850 --> 20:48.020
But...

20:49.730 --> 20:53.150
Please don't be mean to Clarin anymore.

20:57.070 --> 20:59.070
What the hell...

20:59.070 --> 21:00.910
Let's go home, Clarin.

21:01.320 --> 21:04.240
did we just get involved with!?

21:04.830 --> 21:06.660
Let's all go home!

21:10.250 --> 21:11.460
Yesterday afternoon,

21:11.460 --> 21:18.920
the CDF located the hideout of a gang stealing high-grade androids.

21:18.920 --> 21:20.760
and arrested them.

21:21.260 --> 21:24.050
The majority of the androids were confiscated,

21:24.050 --> 21:29.430
but some are thought to have been sold to locations off-island through channels currently being traced.

21:29.430 --> 21:33.150
At the time of their arrest, every member of the crime gang was heavily injured.

21:33.150 --> 21:35.400
Huh? They're beaten up.

21:33.150 --> 21:35.860
Based on the chaotic nature of their testimony,

21:35.860 --> 21:41.910
the group may have experienced some kind of
internal discord or been dealt some sort of punishment.

21:37.110 --> 21:38.110
Man...

21:38.110 --> 21:41.910
Do they have any idea how much trouble it was to clean up their mess?

21:49.000 --> 21:51.250
Visibility restored in the underwater work area.

21:51.250 --> 21:53.080
Switching to visual operation.

21:58.300 --> 22:00.170
Modify the decoy AIs?

22:00.760 --> 22:02.340
Every one of these?

22:02.340 --> 22:03.680
That's right.

22:04.180 --> 22:05.680
Get started right away.

22:06.260 --> 22:11.060
The majority of them meet the uniform standard, but when there's <i>this</i> many of them...

22:11.060 --> 22:12.190
Do it.

22:16.610 --> 22:19.150
Time waits for no one.

22:41.010 --> 22:44.010
Accessing the device named nature

22:44.010 --> 22:47.010
The circuit of infinite synapses

22:47.010 --> 22:47.550
read

22:47.550 --> 22:48.100
write

22:48.100 --> 22:48.760
enter

22:48.760 --> 22:49.390
code

22:49.390 --> 22:52.770
Sharing tools can lead to unavoidable situations

22:52.770 --> 22:55.690
How did you know the androids wanted to go home?

22:53.480 --> 23:04.070
{talk}{this is pandoradio, it'll change each week, ignore this segemnt}

22:55.690 --> 22:58.270
I heard all their voices saying, "I want to go home."

22:58.270 --> 23:00.940
It's possible that was residual data still left in their memory.

23:00.940 --> 23:03.320
Nope, it's the voice of an android's heart.

23:03.320 --> 23:04.070
Impossible.

23:04.070 --> 23:05.450
Saving data

23:05.450 --> 23:06.820
Strengthening predictions

23:06.820 --> 23:09.830
Even my latest updates

23:09.830 --> 23:15.120
can't help explain why you're so nice to me

23:15.120 --> 23:16.710
Error error

23:16.710 --> 23:18.210
parameter

23:18.210 --> 23:21.590
Please help me understand

23:21.590 --> 23:23.760
where these emotions came from.

23:23.760 --> 23:26.930
Find me at the end of this labrynth

23:26.930 --> 23:29.680
of feelings I can no longer control

23:29.680 --> 23:31.680
I understand the concept of emotions

23:31.680 --> 23:35.060
but I can't make any sense of my own

23:35.440 --> 23:38.060
I want to pull out these cords

23:38.400 --> 23:40.820
and head straight to you

23:40.820 --> 23:43.230
I won't come to understand love

23:43.230 --> 23:46.990
without having you here with me

23:51.870 --> 23:54.290
Clarin, thanks for saving me!

23:54.290 --> 23:56.790
Nene's safety is a third-priority matter.

23:56.790 --> 24:01.210
My third-priority matter is to hug and squeeze you!

24:01.210 --> 24:03.050
Squeeze!

24:03.050 --> 24:05.340
I'm glad to see you two are so close.
